      "headline": "Senior Site Reliability Engineer | Observability | Reliability Engineering | Automation | AI Ops | Terraform | Kubernetes | AWS/Azure/GCP",
      "about": "I am a Senior Site Reliability Engineer specializing in observability, reliability engineering, incident management, and automation across AWS, Azure, and GCP environments. My work focuses on improving reliability, monitoring, and operational efficiency for large-scale distributed systems.I have worked extensively on observability platforms, monitoring and alerting strategies, SLO/SLI implementation, incident response, cost optimization, and infrastructure automation using Terraform and Kubernetes-based platforms. I have led initiatives around observability cost optimization, alerting improvements, dashboards, runbooks, and operational readiness for multiple production services.Recently, I have been working on chaos engineering, release anomaly detection, and AI-driven operations, including building an AI-based incident detection and triage system (AI NOC) to improve incident response, reduce alert fatigue, and enhance operational visibility.I enjoy solving reliability and scalability problems, improving incident management processes, and building automation that reduces operational toil and improves system observability. I am particularly interested in reliability engineering, observability platforms, platform engineering, distributed systems, and AIOps.Core areas: Observability, Reliability Engineering, Incident Management, Automation, Chaos Engineering, AI Ops, Terraform, Kubernetes, AWS, Azure, GCP.Open to opportunities in Site Reliability Engineering, Observability Engineering, Platform Engineering, and Reliability Engineering roles.",
